- * ghk: Gunyah kernel launcher -- userspace ABI (stage-2 skeleton).
+ * ghk: Gunyah kernel launcher -- userspace ABI.
  *
  * The anchor process creates the VM with the stock /dev/gunyah ioctls (create, memory, DTB, boot context,
  * vcpu functions, START) and then hands the VM fd and the vcpu fds to /dev/ghk. ghk runs the vcpus in kernel
  * threads that borrow the anchor's mm (the in-tree driver insists on ghvm->mm_s) and services MMIO exits
  * in the kernel. The anchor keeps /dev/ghk open for the life of the VM; closing it stops the vcpu threads.
+ *
+ * ABI 2 (stage 3, crosvm-ghk anchor): serial_irqfd + GHK_LAUNCH_SERIAL_IRQ (edge interrupt of the in-kernel
+ * 16550, an eventfd the anchor registered with GUNYAH_FN_IRQFD), max_run_ms (mandatory kernel-side bound on a
+ * live launch), status.launched / status.flags. Struct sizes are unchanged (120 / 80 bytes); fields carved out
+ * of the old reserved space.
  */
